# Round 18, C2-32 (follows). L §5.14.3: a version known inside a windowed instance's window: "the instance's amount is
# decided by §4.4's rule: HOLE-IMPRECISE where the version changes it, unless the line states windows each"; L §4.4 "One
# rule for every window". g falls in window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-31); v2, known 2026-03-15 inside it, changes only
# other, which g doesn't read: its amount is 100.00 PLN, no hole (q, q2). L4_4_known_inside_window_changes: v2 changes
# amt.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind gifts: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 2026-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input other: money PLN
input w: date

move g: gifts
  on w
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

ask q: g.cash.amount
ask q2: g.cash.amount windows each

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN
  other = 1.00 PLN
  w = window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-31)
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start

version v2
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-03-15
  replace other = 2.00 PLN
=== expect
q: 100.00 PLN
  cut 2026-06-30
q2: 100.00 PLN
  cut 2026-06-30
warning: WARN-UNREAD input other is read by nothing
